8. Privilege Escalation

After obtaining the user flag, I inspected Lennie's `scripts` directory:
cd ~/scripts
ls -la
I found:

planner.sh
startup_list.txt

I inspected planner.sh:
cat planner.sh
It contained:
#!/bin/bash
echo $LIST > /home/lennie/scripts/startup_list.txt
/etc/print.sh

The important part was: /etc/print.sh


I checked the permissions:
Output:
-rwx------ 1 lennie lennie 25 Nov 12 2020 /etc/print.sh
This was significant because **Lennie owned `/etc/print.sh` and could modify it**.

